<article class="env-lemma" id="0462">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0462">Lemma <span data-tag="0462">67.23.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$, $g : Y \to Z$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$. If $g \circ f : X \to Z$ is locally of finite type, then $f : X \to Y$ is locally of finite type. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We can find a diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ U \ar[r] \ar[d] &  V \ar[r] \ar[d] &  W \ar[d] \\  X \ar[r] &  Y \ar[r] &  Z }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $U$, $V$, $W$ are schemes, the vertical arrows are étale and surjective, see Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/02X1" data-tag="02X1">65.11.6</a>. At this point we can use Lemma <a href="/tag/040Y" data-tag="040Y">67.23.4</a> and Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01T8" data-tag="01T8">29.15.8</a> to conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>